Subject: [PATCH] src/lib/EBOOKCharsetConverter.cpp: use C++ true/false

ICU no longer provides the legacy TRUE/FALSE constants, so this 0.1.3 call
site fails to compile with "use of undeclared identifier 'TRUE'" against
icu4c/77.  Upstream fixed exactly this line between 0.1.3 and 0.1.4 (the two
files are otherwise byte-identical), so the patch mirrors upstream instead
of inventing a macro shim.

--- a/src/lib/EBOOKCharsetConverter.cpp
+++ b/src/lib/EBOOKCharsetConverter.cpp
@@ -124,7 +124,7 @@
       m_converterToUTF8.get(), m_converterToUnicode.get(),
       &outText, outText + out.size(), &inText, inText + length,
       nullptr, nullptr, nullptr, nullptr,
-      TRUE, TRUE, &status)
+      true, true, &status)
     ;
     if (status==U_BUFFER_OVERFLOW_ERROR)
     {
